.\" This manpage was written by Carla Valenti <valenti.karla@gmail.com>
.\" and Christian Giessen <cgie@informatik.uni-kiel.de> for tty-clock.
.\" In details the command line options displayed by tty-clock -h as
.\" well as the keyboard commands.
.TH "TTY-CLOCK" "1" "October 2013" "" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
.LP
tty\-clock \- a terminal digital clock
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.LP
\fBtty\-clock [\-iuvsScbtrahDBxn] [\-C [\fI0\-7\fB]] [\-f \fIformat\fB] [\-d \fIdelay\fB] [\-a \fInsdelay\fB] \fB[\-T \fItty\fB] [\-\-theme default|nord]\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.LP
\fItty\-clock\fR displays a simple digital clock on the terminal. Invoked without options
it will display the clock on the upper left corner of the screen on the terminal it was
executed from.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.LP
\fItty\-clock\fR accepts a number of runtime keyboard commands, upper and lower case characters are
treated identically.
.TP
K,J,H,L
vi\-style movement commands to set the position of the displayed clock.
These commands have no effect when the \fBcentered\fR option is set.
.TP
[0\-7]
Select a different color for displaying the clock.
With Nord, select a Nord accent (0 muted, 1 red, 2 green, 3 yellow,
4 blue, 5 purple, 6 frost, 7 white).
.TP
B
Toggles between bold and normal colors.
.TP
X
Toggles displaying a box around the clock. This option is disabled by default.
.TP
C
Toggle the clock's position to \fBcentered\fR.
When set the movement commands are disabled.
.TP
R
Set the clock to \fBrebound\fR along the edges of the terminal.
.TP
S
Display seconds.
.TP
T
Switch time output to the 12\-hour format.
.TP
Q
Quit.
.TP
P
Toggle the Copilot usage display below the date.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.LP
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\fR \fIname\fR
Select default terminal colors or the nord theme. Nord fills the terminal
with a Polar Night background (#2E3440), uses Frost (#88C0D0) for the clock
and filled Copilot bar, Snow Storm (#D8DEE9) for date and usage text, and
muted borders. Exact RGB colors are used when palette changes are supported;
otherwise colors are approximated with the available terminal palette.
With Nord, \fB\-C\fR and keys 0\-7 select Nord accents; text stays light.
An explicit \fB\-C\fR takes precedence over the theme's default Frost accent
regardless of option order.
.TP
\fB\-\-copilot\fR
Show a Copilot consumption progress bar below the date, followed by actual
usage and total allowance on a separate line. Uses the existing GitHub CLI
authentication for github.com. Requires gh on PATH. Credit-based billing shows
credits; legacy billing shows premium requests. Unlimited allowances have no
percentage. Failed refreshes retain the last reading marked stale.
.TP
\fB\-\-copilot-refresh\fR \fIseconds\fR
Set the background quota refresh interval (1 to 86400 seconds, default 60).
Requests time out after 15 seconds. Does not enable the display by itself.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR
Show seconds.
.TP
\fB\-S\fR
Screensaver mode. tty\-clock terminates when any key is pressed.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR
Show box.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR
Set the clock at the center of the terminal.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR \fI[0\-7]\fR
Set the clock color.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR
Use bold colors.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR
Set the hour in 12h format.
.TP
\fB\-u\fR
Use UTC time.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR \fItty\fR
Display the clock on the given \fItty\fR. \fItty\fR must be
a valid character device to which the user has rw access permissions.
(See \fBEXAMPLES\fR)
.TP
\fB\-r\fR
Do rebound the clock.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR \fIformat\fR
Set the date format as described in \fBstrftime(3)\fR.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR
Do not quit the program when the Q key is pressed (or when any
key is pressed while in \fBScreensaver\fR mode). A signal must
be sent to \fItty\-clock\fR in order to terminate its execution. (See \fBEXAMPLES\fR)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Show tty\-clock version.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR
Show some info about tty\-clock.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Show usage information.
.TP
\fB\-D\fR
Hide the date.
.TP
\fB\-B\fR
Enable blinking colon.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR \fIdelay\fR
Set the delay (in seconds) between two redraws of the clock. Default 1s.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR \fInsdelay\fR
Additional delay (in nanoseconds) between two redraws of the clock. Default 0ns.
.SH "COPILOT BUDGET"
.LP
With \fB\-\-copilot\fR, daily usage and a fixed calendar-day budget appear
below the allowance. Days and the assumed first-of-month reset use UTC.
The Today line shows remaining headroom or the percentage over today's budget.
A second usage graph shows today's measured consumption as a percentage of
the estimated daily average. 100% is one average day's usage, not the safe
budget; the bar caps at 100% while the displayed percentage may exceed it.
Incomplete days graph only consumption since the displayed UTC start time.
Missing or zero averages are shown explicitly instead of a percentage.
Incomplete days show unknown daily usage plus consumption since the first
reading's UTC time. Safe avg shows the maximum average daily usage the
remaining allowance supports until reset. Month avg or Recent avg shows
actual consumption and whether it exceeds that safe pace. Forecasts use up
to seven days of observed consumption, falling back to a monthly average
after the first hour. The display reports whether the quota should hold
until reset or estimates an exhaustion date, time and how many days or hours
before reset it will run out.
Est. limit by shows the suggested total quota limit: already consumed usage
plus estimated usage until the displayed reset date at the same average rate,
but never less than the current limit. Its percentage shows the required
increase relative to the current limit; no increase means it is sufficient.
Future-usage and exhaustion estimates use the latest successful measurement.
The display uses a shared left edge with blank rows separating monthly quota,
today's usage and the forecast.
.LP
History is stored privately in
\fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/tty-clock/copilot-history\fR, defaulting to
\fI~/.local/state/tty-clock/copilot-history\fR. No credentials are stored.
Readings near midnight approximate full days, marked ~.
Unwritable history uses session tracking, marked [no save].
Remove the history file when switching GitHub accounts. Forecasts are
estimates and may be affected by delayed API accounting.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.LP
Show a centered Nord clock with seconds:
.IP
$ tty\-clock \-c \-s \-\-theme nord
.LP
Show a centered clock with seconds and Copilot usage:
.IP
$ tty\-clock \-c \-s \-\-copilot
.LP
To invoke
.I tty\-clock
in screensaver mode with the clock display set to rebound and the update
delay set to 1/10th of a second (10 FPS):
.IP
$ tty\-clock \-Sra 100000000 \-d 0
.LP
The following example arranges for \fItty\-clock\fR to be displayed
indefinitely on one of the Virtual Terminals on a Linux system
at boot time using an
.B inittab(5)
entry:
.IP
# /etc/inittab:
.br
9:2345:respawn:/usr/bin/tty\-clock \-c \-n \-T /dev/tty9
.LP
